            "review_title": "Review at Pho Quyen",
            "review_text": "arthurs5\nSydney, Australia110 contributions\n0\nBest Pho in Vietnam\nMay 2017 • Family\nI know this sounds like an extravagant claim in country whose national dish is practically Pho, but its true. I was taken to this restaurant by a girl I met on the bus and briefly helped with her bio-engineering degree. I went back 3 times with different family members and they all thought the same. I've had probably well over 200 different Phos from all over Vietnam, and there are many good ones and many bad ones, but Pho Quyen has the best I've had for both broth flavour and meat texture.. It's not in the tourist area, but is on the road between the airport and large ex-pat community in district 2.It opens for breakfast until 11:30am and for dinner from 4pm to 9:30pm. The price is very reasonable, 45K VND (about $A2.50) for a large bowl with all the different beef cuts.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 10, 2017",
